<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - American Medical Response lowered.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - American Medical Response lowered.</headline>
<text>
<p>--Lehman Brothers downgraded American Medical Response Inc to neutral from buy after the company said late Monday it would be acquired by Laidlaw Inc for US$1.12 billion cash.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Jeffrey Kessler said in a note to clients that the $40 per share offer was a fair price. He recommended investors tender their shares.</p>
<p>--Kessler said the transaction will give Laidlaw a 14 percent market share of the $10 billion healthcare transportation industry.</p>
<p>--Shares of American Medical Response jumped 6-1/4 to 39-1/4.</p>
</text>
